-- title:
--   Right-continuous record regulators carry no Stieltjes mass on nonpositive times
-- statement:
--   For any right-continuous path whose monotone running record M is represented by the supremum over [0,t] and dominates the path, the Stieltjes dividend measure generated by M has no mass on (-∞,0]. The result applies to the post-first-upcrossing future-increment running record without requiring the shifted process to be constructed as another Lévy object.
-- source:
--   Direct missing hνneg hypothesis of map-shift theorem 3093890e-4ed7-4198-8491-5f41d268763c for strong-Markov child 79978d61-9d1f-4b20-b8a5-114797a8e380. Uses proved generic running-record right-continuity f0c2320c and rightLim extension 95b3270f with pending generic Stieltjes support lemma ab1b11d7.

